sterday's report  in The Hollywood Reporter if you didn't  read it basically all you need to know  is that they said that sources told them  that Patty Jenkins and the other writers  met with James Gunn and Peter Safran to  talk about the future of Wonder Woman 3  and gave them some of the script in  which they told her the project was  scrapped and the reason for that is that  it didn't fit into their new plan now  recently James Gunn and Peter saffron  went to Colorado for kind of like a  little Retreat so both of them could  write together the DC Bible that's what  they're calling the road map of what is  to come for DC how everything is going  to be connected so they were literally  planning out the next 10 years of the DC  Universe and apparently Wonder Woman 3  or at least the version of Wonder Woman  3 that they already had done was not a  part of it the article also said that  Man of Steel 2 with Henry Cavill  returning is also unlikely and everybody  was freaking out and was very confused  rightfully so because Henry Cavill just  made his return and just announced that  he was back as Superman we saw him in  Black Adam so everybody's wondering what  is really going on well James Gunn took  to Twitter and he said this so as for  the story yesterday in The Hollywood  Reporter some of it is true some of it  is half true some of it is not true and  some of it we haven't decided yet  whether it's true or not so right away  very very interesting sums true some is  not true some is undecided so right now  they're still kind of working on that  10-year plan we do know that next week  James Gunn and Peter saffron are meeting  with the heads of Warner Brothers  Discovery and it seems like this is the  time where they're going to sort of  finalize the direction that they're  going to be taking with the DCU so some  of these things that were mentioned in  the article might actually depend on how  this meeting is going to go now we'll  Circle back and talk about what I 